<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! library.index.writes ~ the index travels; the bodies stay off every tracked tree

`lares library index <collection> --out <path>` writes the collection's index (one `#/<cid>` slot per entry, origin and licence beside it) to a path the operator tracks. The bodies never move.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ index

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`index` params=`collection/mark-twain out/library/mark-twain.mem ~ write the tracked index of one collection`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ collection · out

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`collection` params=`takes/name needs/required seat/1 as/<collection> ~ the collection`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`out` params=`takes/host-path needs/required ~ where the index lands`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ local

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`local` params=`who/hand ~ writes a host path; this handler checks no ocap`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/refuses`>>

!! refuses ~ usage

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`refusal` name=`usage` params=`cure/[[library.index.writes collection/mark-twain out/library/mark-twain.mem]] ~ no collection named, or no --out`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

